  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Arthur H. del Prado was a Dutch semiconductor entrepreneur who founded ASM and built it into an international equipment group. His expansion created ASM Pacific Technology and helped launch ASML with Philips, strengthening Europe’s chipmaking supply chain. He led ASM for four decades and became known as the father of Europe’s semiconductor equipment industry.",
    "html": "<p>Arthur H. del Prado was a Dutch semiconductor entrepreneur who founded ASM and built it into an international equipment group. His expansion created ASM Pacific Technology and helped launch ASML with Philips, strengthening Europe’s chipmaking supply chain. He led ASM for four decades and became known as the father of Europe’s semiconductor equipment industry.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 54,
